## Chapter 4 — Heuristic State Vector Estimation: United States and China, 2026

### 4.1 Epistemological Status of This Chapter

All estimates in this chapter are (E) — empirical claims about the state of AI infrastructure derived from publicly available primary sources, bounded by explicitly stated uncertainty intervals. They are not precise measurements, not econometrically estimated values, and not conclusions of this dissertation. They are prior distributions intended to serve two purposes: to illustrate the mathematical structure of the CAPI framework with plausible numerical values, and to provide the starting point for the sensitivity analyses of Chapter 6. They must be replaced, in their entirety, by the outputs of the Phase II empirical estimation program before any quantitative conclusion from this framework can be claimed.

