## Chapter 10 — Complete Prescriptive Empirical Calibration Program

This chapter constitutes the most operationally significant contribution of this dissertation for future researchers. It specifies, with the exactness of an experimental protocol, every step that must be executed to transform the theoretical architecture of the preceding chapters into an empirically calibrated, publishable econometric model. No step in this protocol has been executed. Every specification is future-directed.

### 10.1 The Log-Linear Regression Foundation

Taking logarithms of the CAPI functional transforms it into a linear regression model:

ln(CAPI_{nt}) = ln(κ_n) + α · ln(C_{nt}) + β · ln(E_{nt}) + γ · ln(S_{nt}) + δ · ln(R_{nt}) + ε · ln(Λ_{nt}) + u_{nt}

where subscript n ∈ {US, CN} indexes nations, t indexes annual time periods, and u_{nt} ~ N(0, σ²_u) is the regression error. This is a standard log-linear production function regression with estimable coefficients appearing as output elasticities — the foundational insight that transforms the CAPI from a theoretical structure into a statistically estimable model.

The full panel specification incorporating fixed effects is:

ln(Y_{nt}) = β_0 + α · ln(C_{nt}) + β · ln(E_{nt}) + γ · ln(S_{nt}) + δ · ln(R_{nt}) + ε · ln(Λ_{nt}) + η_n + τ_t + u_{nt}

where Y_{nt} is the CAPI proxy variable constructed in Phase I, η_n is the nation fixed effect absorbing κ_n and all Assumption A1 residuals, and τ_t is the time fixed effect capturing global AI advancement trends common to both nations. Given only two nations, standard fixed-effects standard errors are biased; block-bootstrapped standard errors with 10,000 replications blocking at the nation level are mandated.

### 10.2 Phase I: Data Infrastructure and Construct Validation

Phase I is the prerequisite for all subsequent estimation and must be completed before any regression is attempted.

The first task is the assembly of longitudinal dimensional time series for both nations over 2005–2026 at annual frequency. Compute capacity C_{nt} is constructed from the Epoch AI Notable AI Models dataset combined with hyperscaler capital expenditure data deflated by an AI hardware price index, cross-validated against MLPerf training and inference benchmark records. Energy availability E_{nt} is constructed from IEA national data center electricity consumption statistics supplemented by Goldman Sachs and Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory surveys and harmonized to a consistent AI-dedicated capacity definition. Semiconductor sovereignty S_{nt} is constructed via the PCA-BO plus Fuzzy Delphi hybrid weighting procedure of Section 3.4 from TSMC-SMIC-Samsung leading-edge market share data, USPTO citation-weighted patent counts, USGS Critical Minerals statistics, and ASML EUV sales records by geography. Research capital R_{nt} is constructed from Semantic Scholar citation-weighted AI publication counts combined with the Epoch AI talent tracker and normalized against the combined US-China frontier research pool. Software ecosystem depth Λ_{nt} is constructed from a GitHub repository dependency graph analysis applying the PageRank centrality formulation of Section 3.5 and supplemented by PyPI download statistics and HuggingFace model framework deployment shares.

The second task is the construction and validation of the CAPI proxy dependent variable Y_{nt}. The theoretical CAPI has no direct observable counterpart, so a composite proxy must be constructed from frontier benchmark performance, MLPerf training throughput records by national hardware, AI-driven GDP contribution estimates, and defense-relevant AI assessment scores where publicly available. The coefficients φ_k weighting these components are estimated via factor analysis on their correlation structure.

The mandatory validation procedure is the Multitrait-Multimethod Confirmatory Factor Analysis. The MTMM design constructs a latent factor model in which CAPI strategic AI power, general technological capacity, scientific research output, and military capability are specified as distinct latent constructs measured by overlapping observable indicators. Convergent validity is confirmed when the proxy components for strategic AI power correlate more strongly with each other than with indicators of the other constructs. Discriminant validity is confirmed when the correlation between the CAPI latent factor and the general technological capacity factor is below 0.70 — the conventional threshold distinguishing related but distinct constructs from near-collinear ones. If discriminant validity fails — specifically, if the CAPI proxy cannot be statistically distinguished from general technological capacity — the weights φ_k must be respecified to increase the loading on AI-specific capability indicators and reduce the loading on general technology proxies before proceeding to estimation.

The out-of-sample validation procedure requires holding out defense-relevant outcome data from the proxy construction and testing whether the civilian-data CAPI estimate predicts those outcomes via cross-validated regression. Out-of-sample R² and calibration metric reporting constitute the external validity test.

The third task is the assembly of the jump event database through manual extraction from the BIS Federal Register for export control announcements, SemiAnalysis and MLCommons records for hardware generation transitions, and the Epoch AI and ArXiv datasets for algorithmic breakthrough events, supplemented by Lee-Mykland statistical detection on high-frequency proxy series.

### 10.3 Phase II: Preliminary Estimation and Specification Testing

Phase II begins with the Box-Cox specification test. The transformation parameter λ in the generalized Box-Cox model is estimated from the assembled data, and the null hypothesis λ = 0 is tested. Failure to reject the null validates the log-linear baseline specification of Section 10.1 and proceeds to standard NPR estimation. Rejection of the null mandates the SC-GAM coupling specification of Section 3.7.

The pilot NPR estimation applies the expectations-based proxy method to the compute dimension alone, using hyperscaler capital expenditure forecasts as the expectations proxy data. This pilot serves to validate algorithm convergence, calibrate the backfitting tolerance, and produce a preliminary estimate of α for comparison against the heuristic prior of 0.35. Agreement within one standard error constitutes preliminary confirmation of the heuristic hierarchy; disagreement motivates re-examination of the dimensional measurement strategies.

The full five-dimensional NPR estimation follows, recovering (α̂, β̂, γ̂, δ̂, ε̂) with bootstrap-corrected standard errors from the full panel. The Bayesian Synthetic Control is run in parallel on the expanded secondary-power panel to produce reduced-form exponent bounds. The Hausman specification test comparing NPR structural estimates with synthetic control reduced-form bounds determines whether the NPR structural assumptions are validated by the data.

The Andrews structural break test for parameter stability over time tests Assumption A3 using rolling 5-year window regressions. The null of constant elasticities over the 2005–2026 horizon is tested at the 5% level. Rejection mandates the time-varying coefficient extension and endogenous break date estimation. The substantive interpretation of the break date — identifying the moment at which the relative importance of the five dimensions underwent structural change — is itself a significant empirical finding.

### 10.4 Identification Challenges and Prescribed Remedies

Reverse causality between CAPI and research capital must be addressed through instrumental variables: lagged PhD graduation rates in computer science and mathematics (3-year lag) are the prescribed instruments, providing plausibly exogenous variation in the talent pipeline that predates current CAPI levels.

The near-perfect correlation between compute and energy implied by the Compute-Energy Coupling Equation of Proposition 3.1 creates multicollinearity that may prevent individual identification of α and β even when their sum is precisely estimated. The prescribed remedy is to report both individual coefficient estimates with their confidence intervals and the constrained sum α + β with its confidence interval, interpreting the individual estimates cautiously when collinearity diagnostics — variance inflation factors exceeding 10 — indicate identification problems.

The endogeneity of export control shocks to the CAPI ratio — large US advantages may trigger more aggressive export control responses, creating reverse causation from S_CN to the strategic incentive for export controls — must be addressed by instrumenting semiconductor sovereignty shocks with lagged Wassenaar Arrangement meeting schedules and Congressional election cycles as plausibly exogenous timing variation.

The mandated robustness checks before any quantitative conclusion are: re-estimation across all alternative proxy specifications with reported exponent ranges; errors-in-variables correction via LIML; Cook's distance outlier analysis and re-estimation after exclusion of influential observations; model selection among log-linear, translog, and extended coupling specifications via AIC, BIC, and cross-validated log-likelihood; and a Monte Carlo simulation validation confirming that the estimation procedure recovers known parameters from data generated by the theoretical model.

### 10.5 Phase III: Jump-Diffusion Calibration and Monte Carlo Simulation

The Bayesian Hierarchical Poisson-Gamma posteriors for jump intensities and magnitude distributions are estimated from the jump event database assembled in Phase I, with the Wassenaar, Congressional, and CCP instruments as covariates. Posteriors for all five shock categories are integrated into the full Monte Carlo simulation protocol specified in Section 9.4. The distributional output of this phase — the full first-passage time density for T* — replaces the deterministic estimate of Chapter 6 as the framework's primary convergence characterization.

### 10.6 Phase IV: Cooperative Dynamics Estimation and Optimal Investment

The cooperation coefficient μ is estimated from historical technology cooperation episodes using the cooperative Lotka-Volterra structural model in panel regression. The Pontryagin maximum principle is applied to solve for the optimal investment schedule allocating a fixed total budget I_total(t) across the five CAPI dimensions to maximize CAPI(N, T) over a given planning horizon T. This optimal control solution constitutes the framework's primary policy-relevant output.

### 10.7 Expected Outcomes and Scientific Implications

If empirical estimation confirms α > β > γ > δ > ε, the heuristic hierarchy is validated and current compute-focused investment strategies receive empirical support. If β exceeds α after energy constraint binding, the energy bottleneck is more severe than the hardware bottleneck and optimal investment should redirect toward grid expansion. If γ substantially exceeds its heuristic prior, export controls are structurally more damaging to Chinese AI capacity than current models assume. If θ is statistically significant and large, the DeepSeek-type algorithmic efficiency path is generalizable and represents a systematic strategic vulnerability in compute-focused national AI strategies. Each of these outcome scenarios has clear implications for investment prioritization, and the disambiguation between them is precisely the irreplaceable contribution of empirical calibration.

