B.8 Proof of Proposition 9.1 (Log-Normal CAPI Distribution)

Proposition: Under the GBM component alone (no jumps):

\ln\left(\frac{\text{CAPI}_t}{\text{CAPI}_0}\right) \sim \mathcal{N}\left((g - \sigma^2/2)t, \sigma^2 t\right)

Proof:

The stochastic differential equation $d\text{CAPI}_t = g \cdot \text{CAPI}_t dt + \sigma \cdot \text{CAPI}_t dW_t$ is solved via Itô's lemma. Define $Y_t = \ln \text{CAPI}_t$. By Itô's lemma:

dY_t = \frac{1}{\text{CAPI}_t} d\text{CAPI}_t - \frac{1}{2} \frac{1}{\text{CAPI}_t^2} (d\text{CAPI}_t)^2

= (g dt + \sigma dW_t) - \frac{1}{2}\sigma^2 dt = (g - \sigma^2/2) dt + \sigma dW_t

Integrating from 0 to $t$:

Y_t - Y_0 = (g - \sigma^2/2)t + \sigma(W_t - W_0)

Since $W_t - W_0 \sim \mathcal{N}(0,t)$, we have:

Y_t - Y_0 \sim \mathcal{N}((g - \sigma^2/2)t, \sigma^2 t)

Exponentiating yields the log-normal distribution. $\square$

