Appendix C: Complete Stochastic Analysis and Jump-Diffusion Derivations

C.1 Full SDE Specification with Jumps

The complete CAPI jump-diffusion process is:

d\text{CAPI}_t = g \cdot \text{CAPI}_t dt + \sigma_0 \cdot \text{CAPI}_t dW_t + \text{CAPI}_{t^-} \int_{\mathbb{R}} (e^y - 1) \tilde{N}(dt, dy)

where:

· $g$: deterministic drift rate (from Chapter 5 dynamics)
· $\sigma_0$: baseline diffusion volatility
· $W_t$: standard Wiener process
· $\tilde{N}(dt, dy)$: compensated Poisson random measure with intensity measure $\nu(dy)dt = \lambda \cdot f_J(y) dy dt$
· $\lambda$: jump arrival intensity (events per year)
· $f_J(y)$: jump size distribution in log-returns

The jump term captures five categorized shock types, each with its own intensity $\lambda_k$ and jump distribution $F_{J,k}$:

Shock Category Symbol Intensity Jump Distribution
Positive Compute $\lambda_C$ 0.3–0.5 yr⁻¹ $J \sim \text{LogN}(\mu_C, \sigma_C^2)$
Negative Semiconductor $\lambda_S$ 0.1–0.3 yr⁻¹ $J \sim \text{BetaNeg}(a_S, b_S)$
Positive Algorithmic $\lambda_A$ 0.2–0.4 yr⁻¹ $J \sim \text{LogN}(\mu_A, \sigma_A^2)$
Energy Infrastructure $\lambda_E$ 0.05–0.15 yr⁻¹ $J \sim \text{GammaNeg}(k_E, \theta_E)$
Geopolitical Discontinuity $\lambda_G$ 0.02–0.08 yr⁻¹ $J \sim \text{MixtureNormal}$

