C.4 Complete Monte Carlo Simulation Algorithm

Algorithm C.2 (CAPI Convergence Monte Carlo):

Input:

· Initial state vectors $\mathbf{X}_{US}(0), \mathbf{X}_{CN}(0)$ with uncertainty distributions
· Estimated drift vectors $\mathbf{g}_{US}, \mathbf{g}_{CN}$ with parameter uncertainty
· Diffusion matrix $\Sigma$ (5×5 covariance of dimensional growth rates)
· Calibrated jump parameters $\{(\lambda_k, F_{J,k})\}_{k=1}^5$ for both nations
· Simulation horizon $T_{\max} = 50$ years
· Number of trajectories $N = 10,000$

Algorithm:

```
For i = 1 to N:
    t = 0
    Draw initial states from posterior distributions
    While t < T_max:
        // Continuous evolution (Euler-Maruyama step)
        For each dimension d:
            dX_d = g_d(X) * dt + σ_d * sqrt(dt) * ε_d
        // Jump check (thinning method)
        For each shock category k:
            Draw U ~ Uniform(0,1)
            If U < λ_k * dt:
                Draw J from F_{J,k}
                Apply jump to relevant dimension(s)
        Update state vector
        t += dt
        Check convergence: if CAPI_CN(t) >= CAPI_US(t):
            T*[i] = t
            Break
    If t >= T_max:
        T*[i] = Inf  // Censored observation
```

Output: Empirical distribution of $T^*$ including:

· $\hat{\mathbb{E}}[T^* | T^* < \infty]$
· $\widehat{\text{Median}}[T^*]$
· $\widehat{P}(T^* \leq 10), \widehat{P}(T^* \leq 20), \widehat{P}(T^* \leq 30), \widehat{P}(T^* \leq 50)$
· $\widehat{P}(T^* = \infty)$ (probability of no convergence within horizon)
· 95% credible intervals

