C.5 Kernel Density Estimation for First Passage Time

The first passage time density is estimated via kernel smoothing with boundary correction:

\hat{f}_{T^*}(t) = \frac{1}{Nh} \sum_{i: T_i^* < \infty} K\left(\frac{t - T_i^*}{h}\right) \cdot w_i

where:

· $K(\cdot)$: Epanechnikov kernel (optimal for mean integrated squared error)
· $h$: bandwidth selected via Sheather-Jones plug-in method
· $w_i$: importance weights if importance sampling is used for rare events
· Boundary correction at $t = 0$ via reflection method

