D.2 Bayesian Synthetic Control: Implementation Details

Algorithm D.2 (Multi-Outcome Bayesian Synthetic Control):

Donor pool: Nations $\mathcal{D} = \{\text{KR}, \text{JP}, \text{EU}, \text{IN}, \text{UK}, \ldots\}$ with at least 10 years of AI infrastructure data.

Model:

\mathbf{Y}_t^{(0)} = \mathbf{W} \mathbf{Y}_t^{(D)} + \boldsymbol{\varepsilon}_t

where:

· $\mathbf{Y}_t^{(0)}$: $5 \times 1$ vector of CAPI dimensions for target nation (counterfactual without treatment)
· $\mathbf{Y}_t^{(D)}$: $5 \times |\mathcal{D}|$ matrix of donor outcomes
· $\mathbf{W}$: $5 \times 5 \times |\mathcal{D}|$ weight tensor (dimension-specific weights)
· $\boldsymbol{\varepsilon}_t \sim \mathcal{N}(0, \Sigma)$

Prior specification:

\text{vec}(\mathbf{W}) \sim \mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0}, \tau^2 \mathbf{I})


\Sigma \sim \text{InverseWishart}(\nu_0, \mathbf{S}_0)


\tau^2 \sim \text{InverseGamma}(a_0, b_0)

MCMC sampling: Hamiltonian Monte Carlo with No-U-Turn Sampler, 4 chains, 2,000 warmup iterations, 4,000 sampling iterations per chain. Convergence assessed via $\hat{R} < 1.01$ and effective sample size > 400.

Output: Posterior distribution of synthetic weights $\mathbf{W}$, from which the counterfactual CAPI trajectory for each nation under alternative policy regimes is constructed. The reduced-form exponent bounds are derived from the relationship between dimensional gaps and CAPI gaps in the donor pool.

