D.7 Bayesian Hierarchical Poisson-Gamma for Jump Parameters

Model D.1 (Hierarchical Poisson-Gamma):

Level 1 (within shock category):

N_k(t) \sim \text{Poisson}(\lambda_k \Delta t)

where $N_k(t)$ is the number of type-$k$ shocks in interval $(t, t+\Delta t]$.

Level 2 (intensity parameterization):

\ln \lambda_{kt} = \mu_k + \boldsymbol{\alpha}_k' \mathbf{X}_t + \eta_k

where:

· $\mathbf{X}_t$ includes Wassenaar meeting cycles, US election cycles, CCP Politburo Standing Committee cycles
· $\eta_k \sim \mathcal{N}(0, \sigma_k^2)$ captures residual variation

Level 3 (hierarchical priors):

\mu_k \sim \mathcal{N}(\mu_0, \tau_0^2)


\boldsymbol{\alpha}_k \sim \mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0}, \sigma_\alpha^2 \mathbf{I})


\sigma_k^2 \sim \text{InverseGamma}(a_\sigma, b_\sigma)

Jump magnitude distributions: Within category $k$, jump sizes (in log returns) are modeled as:

J_{k,i} \sim F_{J,k}(\boldsymbol{\phi}_k)

with category-appropriate distributions and hierarchical priors on parameters $\boldsymbol{\phi}_k$.

MCMC implementation: Stan probabilistic programming language, 4 chains, 2000 warmup + 4000 sampling iterations. Posterior predictive checks via simulation-based calibration (Talts et al., 2018).

