Appendix F: Formal Problem Statements and Solution Approaches

F.1 Problem 12.1: Optimal Investment Schedule

Formal Statement:

Given the CAPI dynamical system:

\dot{X}_i(t) = \gamma_i \cdot I_i(t - \tau_i) - \delta_i X_i(t) + \text{jump terms}

with control variables $I_i(t) \geq 0$ (investment in dimension $i$) and total budget constraint $\sum_i I_i(t) \leq I_{\text{total}}(t)$, find the investment schedule $\{I_i^*(t)\}_{t=0}^T$ that maximizes:

\text{CAPI}(T) = \kappa \cdot \prod_i X_i(T)^{\alpha_i}

subject to the dynamics and constraints.

Solution Approach (Pontryagin Maximum Principle):

The current-value Hamiltonian is:

\mathcal{H} = \sum_i p_i [\gamma_i I_i - \delta_i X_i] + \lambda \left(I_{\text{total}} - \sum_i I_i\right)

where $p_i$ are costate variables.

First-order conditions:

\frac{\partial \mathcal{H}}{\partial I_i} = p_i \gamma_i - \lambda = 0 \implies I_i^* > 0 \text{ only if } p_i \gamma_i = \lambda

Complementary slackness: $I_i^* = 0$ if $p_i \gamma_i < \lambda$.

Costate dynamics:

\dot{p}_i = -\frac{\partial \mathcal{H}}{\partial X_i} + r p_i = \delta_i p_i + r p_i = (\delta_i + r) p_i

(with discount rate $r$ if applicable, or $r = 0$ in baseline).

Transversality condition: $p_i(T) = \alpha_i \cdot \text{CAPI}(T) / X_i(T)$ (marginal value of final-period dimension $i$).

Computational solution: Two-point boundary value problem solved via shooting method or collocation. Given the low dimensionality ($n = 5$), direct transcription with nonlinear programming (IPOPT solver) is tractable for Phase IV implementation.

