F.2 Problem 12.3: Full Convergence Time Distribution

Formal Statement:

For the bivariate jump-diffusion:

d\begin{pmatrix} X_A \\ X_B \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} g_A X_A \\ g_B X_B \end{pmatrix} dt + \begin{pmatrix} \sigma_A X_A & 0 \\ \rho\sigma_B X_B & \sqrt{1-\rho^2}\sigma_B X_B \end{pmatrix} d\mathbf{W}_t + \text{jump terms}

derive the distribution of $T^* = \inf\{t: X_B(t) \geq X_A(t)\}$.

Solution approach via Fokker-Planck equation:

Let $Z_t = \ln(X_A/X_B)$ with dynamics:

dZ_t = \mu_Z dt + \sigma_Z dW_t + \int_{\mathbb{R}} y \tilde{N}_Z(dt, dy)

The probability $P(t,z) = \mathbb{P}(T^* > t | Z_0 = z)$ satisfies the partial integro-differential equation:

\frac{\partial P}{\partial t} = \mu_Z \frac{\partial P}{\partial z} + \frac{\sigma_Z^2}{2} \frac{\partial^2 P}{\partial z^2} + \lambda \int_{\mathbb{R}} [P(t, z+y) - P(t,z)] f_J(y) dy

with boundary condition $P(t, 0) = 0$ (absorption at convergence $Z_t = 0$) and initial condition $P(0, z) = 1$ for $z > 0$.

The first passage time density is $f_{T^*}(t) = -\partial P(t, z_0)/\partial t$ where $z_0 = \ln(r)$.

Numerical solution: Finite difference method with Crank-Nicolson time stepping for the diffusion part and explicit treatment of the integral jump term. Grid: $z \in [0, z_{\max}]$ with $N_z = 1000$ points, time step $\Delta t = 0.001$ years, horizon $T = 50$ years.

