Appendix G: Sensitivity Analysis Derivations

G.1 Full Partial Derivative Matrix for T*

The deterministic convergence time $T^* = \ln(r)/\Delta g$ depends on the CAPI ratio $r$ and growth differential $\Delta g$, which in turn depend on all five dimensional ratios and growth rate components.

Definition: Let $r_i = X_i^{US}/X_i^{CN}$ be the dimensional ratio for dimension $i$, and $\Delta g_i = g_i^{CN} - g_i^{US}$ be the dimensional growth differential.

Then:

r = \prod_i r_i^{\alpha_i}


\Delta g = \sum_i \alpha_i \Delta g_i


T^* = \frac{\sum_i \alpha_i \ln r_i}{\sum_i \alpha_i \Delta g_i}

Partial derivatives:

\frac{\partial T^*}{\partial \alpha_k} = \frac{\ln r_k \cdot \Delta g - \Delta g_k \cdot \ln r}{(\Delta g)^2}

\frac{\partial T^*}{\partial \ln r_k} = \frac{\alpha_k}{\Delta g}

\frac{\partial T^*}{\partial \Delta g_k} = -\frac{\alpha_k \ln r}{(\Delta g)^2}

Numerical evaluation under heuristic priors:

Parameter Value $\partial T^*/\partial$ Elasticity
$\alpha$ (Compute) 0.35 $(\ln(3.48) \cdot 0.010 - (-0.15) \cdot 0.727)/(0.010)^2 = 2344$ 0.113
$\beta$ (Energy) 0.25 $(\ln(2.04) \cdot 0.010 - 0.13 \cdot 0.727)/(0.010)^2 = -233$ -0.008
$\gamma$ (Semiconductor) 0.20 $(\ln(1.39) \cdot 0.010 - 0.10 \cdot 0.727)/(0.010)^2 = -395$ -0.011
