The elasticity column shows the percentage change in $T^*$ for a 1% change in each exponent. These small elasticities for $\beta$ through $\varepsilon$ indicate that $T^*$ is primarily sensitive to $\alpha$ and to the growth differential components, not to the exact exponent values. This is a robust structural property of the multiplicative formulation.

